@startuml
title SplitSmart - Expense Submission, Review, and Balance Update
start
:User enters amount, date, description, split, participants and optional receipt;
:Swing adapter sends SubmitExpense request;
:Load group and membership through ports;
:Validate positive amount;
:Validate submitter is payer and participant;
:Validate split and compute shares;
if (Valid?) then (yes)
  :Create expense with PENDING_REVIEW status;
  :Persist expense and participants;
  :Request expense-created notification;
  :Show pending review status;
  :Await reviewer action;
  :Load pending expense and reviewer context;
  :Apply configured reviewer authorization;
  if (Authorized and expense pending?) then (yes)
    if (Decision?) then (Approve)
      :Record approval event;
      :Set expense status to APPROVED;
      :Persist review decision;
      :Recalculate pairwise balances from approved expenses and payments;
      :Present updated balance summary;
    else (Reject)
      :Record rejection event;
      :Set expense status to REJECTED;
      :Persist review decision;
      :Keep expense excluded from balances;
      :Present rejection status;
    endif
  else (no)
    :Reject review command and preserve pending state;
    :Present authorization/state error;
  endif
else (no)
  :Return validation errors;
  :Do not persist a submitted expense;
endif
stop

note right
  Open specification questions: reviewer authorization,
  whether one or multiple approvals are required,
  creator self-approval, and behavior after rejection.
  Approval alone is modeled as the balance gate because
  only approved expenses affect balances in the data model.
end note
@enduml
